 <div class="feature-topline"><span>SYSAL / IMPERIAL COLLEGE LONDON</span><span>RESEARCH LABORATORY</span></div>
 <section class="feature-opening">
  <div class="feature-statement"><div class="feature-overline">SYSTEMS &amp; ALGORITHMS LABORATORY</div><h1>Designing trustworthy<br/>autonomous systems<span class="feature-dot">.</span></h1><p class="feature-lead">Learning, control and decision-making for the physical world.</p><p class="feature-description">We develop algorithms and engineered systems that connect learning, decision-making and the physical world. Our research spans trustworthy autonomy, planning under uncertainty, intelligent communications, digital fabrication and privacy-preserving sensing.</p><div class="feature-actions"><a href="/research/">Explore our research ↗</a></div></div>
  <article class="feature-lead-feature"><div class="feature-feature-meta"><span>01 / FEATURED RESEARCH</span><span>IEEE TASE 2025 · IROS 2025 PRESENTATION</span></div><a href="https://alex-yanranwang.github.io/ConsDRED-SMPC.html"><div class="feature-consdred-motion"><video autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="metadata" poster="/research/consdred-demo-still.jpg" aria-label="ConsDRED quadrotor flight demonstration with trajectory visualisation"><source src="/research/consdred-loop.mp4" type="video/mp4"/></video><img class="feature-consdred-reduced" src="/research/consdred-demo-still.jpg" alt="ConsDRED quadrotor flight demonstration still"/></div><div class="feature-photo-credit">ConsDRED flight demonstration · Wang &amp; Boyle · IEEE TASE 2025</div><h2>Reliable quadrotor control under uncertain aerodynamic forces <span>↗</span></h2></a><p>ConsDRED combines distributional reinforcement learning with stochastic model predictive control to track trajectories while respecting constraints.</p><div class="feature-feature-links"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1109/TASE.2024.3432405">Paper ↗</a><a href="https://alex-yanranwang.github.io/ConsDRED-SMPC.html">Project ↗</a><a href="/research/consdred/">Overview ↗</a></div></article>
 </section>
 <section class="feature-research" aria-label="Selected research">
 <div class="feature-research-grid">
  <article class="feature-research-awavo"><div class="feature-item-index">02 / AWaVO <span>ICML 2024</span></div><a href="https://alex-yanranwang.github.io/AWaVO.html"><img src="/research/awavo-figure-1.png" alt="AWaVO paper Figure 1: graphical model for constrained reinforcement learning showing parameter identification and policy updating" loading="lazy"/><div class="feature-image-source">Wang, Qian &amp; Boyle · ICML 2024 · Figure 1: graphical model for constrained RL</div></a><h3>Interpretable decisions under uncertainty</h3><p>Probabilistic constrained reinforcement learning with formal interpretability, evaluated in real quadrotor flight.</p><div class="feature-inline-links"><a href="https://proceedings.mlr.press/v235/wang24bf.html">Paper ↗</a><a href="https://alex-yanranwang.github.io/AWaVO.html">Project ↗</a></div></article>
  <article class="feature-research-icml"><div class="feature-item-index">03 / FUNCTIONAL INTERPRETABILITY <span>ICML 2025</span></div><a href="https://proceedings.mlr.press/v267/soligo25a.html"><img src="/research/icml-modularity-home.png" alt="Research figure from Soligo, Ferraro and Boyle illustrating functional modularity in reinforcement learning policies" loading="lazy"/><div class="feature-image-source">Soligo, Ferraro &amp; Boyle · ICML 2025 · figure extract</div></a><h3>Finding function in learned policies</h3><p>Inducing and detecting neural modules, then testing their functional roles through interventions on learned policy networks.</p><div class="feature-inline-links"><a href="https://proceedings.mlr.press/v267/soligo25a.html">Paper ↗</a><a href="https://sites.google.com/view/mod-xrl/home">Project ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/annasoligo/BIXRL">Code ↗</a></div></article>
 </div></section>
 <section class="strand-research-breadth" aria-label="Research across SysAL">
  <article class="strand-breadth-item"><div class="feature-item-index">MISSION PLANNING / OPTIMISATION</div><h2>Planning under uncertainty</h2><p>Mission-level routing, resource allocation and adaptive replanning as operating conditions change.</p><p>Research in <em>European Journal of Operational Research</em> and <em>IEEE Internet of Things Journal</em>.</p><a href="/research/#planning-heading">Explore planning research ↗</a></article>
  <article class="strand-breadth-item"><div class="feature-item-index">LEARNING / WIRELESS COMMUNICATIONS</div><h2>Learning for intelligent communications</h2><p>Multi-agent learning, aerial networks and reconfigurable wireless systems, with an emphasis on performance, fairness and explainability.</p><p>Research in <em>IEEE TMLCN</em>, <em>Ad Hoc Networks</em> and <em>IEEE OJ-COMS</em>.</p><a href="/research/#communications-heading">Explore communications research ↗</a></article>
  <article class="strand-breadth-item"><div class="feature-item-index">3D-PRINTED ELECTRONICS / DIGITAL FABRICATION</div><a href="/research/#fabrication-heading"><img src="/research/mm-open5x-original.png" alt="Multi-axis, multi-material printing of conformal electronics, from the MM-Open5x research" loading="lazy"/></a><h2>3D-printed electronics and digital fabrication</h2><p>Designing and fabricating functional electronics on curved and freeform surfaces—from thermoformed circuits to conformal antennas and multi-layer power electronics. Open5x and MM-Open5x provide open platforms for multi-axis, multi-material printing.</p><a href="/research/#fabrication-heading">Explore fabrication research ↗</a></article>
  <article class="strand-breadth-item"><div class="feature-item-index">PRIVACY / TRUSTWORTHY SENSING</div><h2>Towards private and trustworthy sensing</h2><p>Understanding and limiting unintended inference from sensor data, including paralinguistic information carried by speech.</p><p>Research published in ACM TOPS, Interspeech and CCW.</p><a href="/research/#privacy-heading">Explore sensing research ↗</a></article>
 </section>
